  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Given \\(\\dfrac{\\log a}{p}=\\dfrac{\\log b}{q}=\\dfrac{\\log c}{r}=\\log x,\\) all logarithms to the same base and \\(x\\ne1.\\) If \\(\\dfrac{b^2}{ac}=x^y,\\) then \\(y\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{q^2}{p+r}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{p+r}{2q}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2q-p-r\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2q-pr\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(q^2-pr\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1967-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The given equalities imply \\(a=x^p,\\) \\(b=x^q,\\) and \\(c=x^r.\\) Therefore \\[ \\frac{b^2}{ac} =x^{2q-p-r}. \\] Since this is \\(x^y\\) and \\(x\\ne1,\\) we have \\(y=2q-p-r.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite the logarithmic equalities as \\(a=x^p,\\) \\(b=x^q,\\) and \\(c=x^r\\)",
        "Substitute those powers into \\(\\frac{b^2}{ac}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
